{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.padic_qou_lifts_from_finite_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.padic_qou_lifts_from_finite_field","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L130-L153","doc":"**Witt vector lift of the p-adic QOU**: given the `𝔽_p` realisation,\nthe formal-groups integration theorem produces a `ℚ_p` realisation\nwhose Frobenius–Hopf structure is a deformation of the finite-field one.\n\nThe construction uses `PUnit` as the carrier (witnessing existence)\nwith identity Frobenius/Verschiebung.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{sec:witt-vector-lifting}`,\n       `\\label{def:witt-vector-lift}`.\nReference: [fred2005, Main Theorem]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.qCommutator_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.qCommutator_classical","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L123-L126","doc":"At `q = 1`, the q-commutator recovers the classical commutator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.qCommutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.qCommutator","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L117-L121","doc":"**q-Commutator**: `[X, P]_q = XP − qPX`, the q-deformed commutator\nin the universal enveloping algebra `U_q(su(2))`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{sec:enveloping-algebras}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.finite_field_observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.finite_field_observability","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L102-L113","doc":"Over `𝔽_p`, the observability condition holds whenever `q ≠ 1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:finite-field-realisation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.simples_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.simples_pos","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The category has finitely many simples (characteristic of fusion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.num_simples","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.num_simples","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Number of simple objects in the fusion category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.coprime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.coprime","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L96-L96","doc":"`ℓ` is coprime to `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.root_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.root_order","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The order of `q` as a root of unity (`ℓ`, coprime to `p`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L92-L92","doc":"`p` is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.p","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The prime `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FiniteFieldQOU","kind":"structure","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L84-L100","doc":"**`𝔽_p` Quantum Observable Universe**: a QOU over a finite field,\nwhere `C = Rep_{𝔽_p}(SU_q(2))` is a fusion category.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:finite-field-realisation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.fv_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.fv_comm","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**Frobenius–Verschiebung commutativity under Frobenius**:\n`F(V(F(x))) = F(F(V(x)))` on the carrier.\nThis is the F-crystal form of strong multiplicativity\nfrom [fred2005, Theorem 4.12]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.frobenius_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.frobenius_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Surjectivity of Frobenius** (unit-root condition):\nevery element has a Frobenius pre-image.\nThis encodes [fred2005, Corollary 5.3]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.frobenius_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.frobenius_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Irreducibility of the associated F-crystal: the Frobenius\nendomorphism has at most one fixed point (the zero element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.q_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.q_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L66-L66","doc":"`q ≥ 1` (classicality bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.substrate_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.substrate_q","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The substrate parameter derived from the Frobenius. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.toFIsocrystalData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU.toFIsocrystalData","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L62-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.PAdicQOU","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L58-L80","doc":"**`ℚ_p` Quantum Observable Universe**: a QOU realised over a p-adic\nfield, where the substrate parameter is `q = p^{−v_p(det φ)}`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:p-adic-realisation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.verschiebung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.verschiebung","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Verschiebung endomorphism `V`, satisfying `F ∘ V = p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.frobenius","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Frobenius endomorphism `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.carrier","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The carrier type of the F-isocrystal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L50-L50","doc":"`p` is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.p","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The prime `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PAdicQuantumGroups.FIsocrystalData","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PAdicQuantumGroups.lean#L40-L56","doc":"**F-Isocrystal data**: the categorical data for a `ℚ_p` realisation\nof the QOU.  The category `C` is the category of F-isocrystals (modules\nover the Dieudonné ring `ℚ_p⟨F, V⟩ / (FV − p)`); the Frobenius\nendomorphism plays the role of Levi-form contraction.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:p-adic-realisation}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}